      "title": "OpenAI’s Medicare attack has exposed Australia’s ‘tech debt’. Fixing it could bring a big bill for taxpayers",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/03/openais-medicare-attack-has-exposed-australias-tech-debt-fixing-it-could-bring-a-big-bill-for-taxpayers",
      "description": "<p>Home affairs department orders all federal government agencies to conduct review of ‘legacy technology’ amid fallout from AI agent hacks </p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Australian government faces significant “tech debt” that could bring a big bill for taxpayers after the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/24/openai-agent-hacked-medicare-australia-what-we-know-so-far-ntwnfb\">OpenAI Medicare breach</a>, as government agencies will need to fortify their defences against future attacks by AI agents.</p><p>This week, the home affairs department ordered all federal government agencies to conduct a “legacy technology stocktake” that requires a plan for each agency to “reduce legacy technology systems” to a level within the agency’s risk tolerance and appetite, <a href=\"https://www.protectivesecurity.gov.au/system/files/2026-09/pspf-direction-002-2026_0.pdf\">the direction stated</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/03/openais-medicare-attack-has-exposed-australias-tech-debt-fixing-it-could-bring-a-big-bill-for-taxpayers\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T15:00:13"
    },
    {
      "title": "Bruce Baird, former federal Liberal MP and NSW minister, dies aged 84",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/bruce-baird-former-federal-liberal-mp-and-nsw-minister-dies-aged-84",
      "description": "<p>Baird, father of former NSW premier Mike Baird and journalist Julia Baird, helped win the Olympics for Sydney</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Bruce Baird, a former federal Liberal MP and deputy leader of the party’s New South Wales branch, has died aged 84.</p><p>Baird, who also served as the NSW transport minister from 1988 to 1995, is the father of former state premier Mike Baird, the ABC journalist Julia Baird, and the marketing executive Steve Baird.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/bruce-baird-former-federal-liberal-mp-and-nsw-minister-dies-aged-84\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T13:03:49"
    },
    {
      "title": "OpenAI disclose another hack on government department in Australia",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/02/openai-disclose-another-hack-on-government-department-in-australia",
      "description": "<p>Attack accessing historical data on bushfires occurred in June but not disclosed by the tech company until Thursday</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Artificial intelligence company OpenAI has disclosed another unauthorised hack on a government department in Australia.</p><p>In June, an OpenAI agent hacked into a New South Wales state government department and accessed historical non-public data on bushfires without authorisation.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/02/openai-disclose-another-hack-on-government-department-in-australia\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T10:00:05"
    },
    {
      "title": "Activists plan legal action against police ban on entering security zone near Perth weapons expo",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/activists-plan-legal-action-against-police-ban-on-entering-security-zone-near-perth-weapons-expo",
      "description": "<p>Under new WA laws anyone who defies an exclusion order could face a maximum $36,000 fine and three years in prison</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Activists and a Greens MP have threatened legal action after the Western Australia police banned at least 12 people entering a designated security area where the Land Forces weapons expo will be held in Perth from 6 October.</p><p>The police used special powers given to them by the WA government last month to ban the activists from entering the area surrounding the Perth Convention and Exhibition Centre.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/02/activists-plan-legal-action-against-police-ban-on-entering-security-zone-near-perth-weapons-expo\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T08:31:55"
